cabal-version:      2.4
name:               http-client
version:            0.7.19
synopsis:           WASI stub: HTTP is unavailable in a browser
description:
    A drop-in replacement for the @http-client@ package used when building
    hledger for wasm32-wasi.
    .
    Nothing in the built code sends a request: the only caller is @req@'s stub,
    which throws, and the only hledger module that mentions any of this is the
    @setup@ command's version check. This package exists purely so the exception
    types @setup@ matches on still have definitions.
    .
    Together with the @req@ stub this removes @http-client@'s own C dependencies
    (@network@'s sockets, @zlib@) from the build plan. See
    @../req-stub/req.cabal@.
    .
    The version number matches the real @http-client@ so hledger's version
    bounds are satisfied unchanged.
    .
    The module interface mirrors the MIT-licensed @http-client@ package by
    Michael Snoyman and contributors.
license:            MIT
build-type:         Simple
category:           Network

library
    exposed-modules:  Network.HTTP.Client
    build-depends:    base >=4 && <5, bytestring, http-types
    hs-source-dirs:   .
    default-language: Haskell2010
